      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mikekinney@Mikes-MacBook-Pro.local",
        "date": "2026-11-10T07:12:04Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(post): a PathPilot plasma post for the Tormach 1300PL\n\ntormach-plasma.cps (\"Tormach PathPilot Plasma\", the first PLASMA_POSTS\nentry) voices a plasma profile in PathPilot's plasma words, from\nUM10720 §6.2-6.3 and §7.1-7.2 and the PathPilot Post Processor\nGuidelines: G20/G21 per the machine, G64 P0.005 Q0.005 (inches), the\nwork offset, G43 H1, G30; per contour G0 X Y to the pierce point, M200\n(AutoFS), M207/M208/M209 when the op states them, G15, G16, the XY cut\n(G41.1/G42.1 D<kerf> and G40 under control compensation; no F under\nAutoFS), M205, G30; then M30. No Z, S, M3-M9, M6 or % is written.\nRefused by name: a non-plasma op, a Plasma Profile path with no plasma\nrecord, an rpm, coolant, a rotary or tilt, a Z cutting move, a cycle,\na machine not declared plasma.\n\nThe stream carries the torch: PLASMA / TORCH ON / TORCH OFF records\n(the .cl v5 records without their \"; \", one reader for both), dumped\naround each span, with the hooks onPlasma / onTorchOn / onTorchOff and\nan engine torch law (no torch without a header, no ON while lit, no\nrapid while lit, nothing left lit; a script without the torch hooks -\nevery milling post - is refused). machine.kind reaches the script.\n\nGoldens: nc/tormach-plasma/plasma_plate_with_holes{,_mm,_control}.nc.\nDecisions: docs/decisions/671-plasma-post.md.\n\nFixes #671\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL",
